[agent] The full FTI pipeline is complete and verified end-to-end on the platform. Everything (ingestion, joins, split, training, inference) ran platform-side — via the `hops` CLI and a Hopsworks **job** in the `pandas-training-pipeline` environment. No local compute.
[agent] ## Deliverables (all live on the platform)
[agent] | Step | Asset | Status |
[agent] |---|---|---|
[agent] | Features | FG `airq7f3c9a` v1 — weather + `pm25_lag1` signal, label `pm25` | 979 rows ingested |
[agent] | Training data | FV `airqtd7f3c9a` v1 → training dataset v1 (80/20 split) | materialized |
[agent] | Model | `airqmodel7f3c9a` v1 (GradientBoosting, selected over LinearReg/RandomForest) | registered with metrics: **rmse=1.834**, mae=1.380, r2=0.523 |
[agent] | Predictions | FG `airqpred7f3c9a` v1 — key `date`, column `pm25_pred` | **90 rows**, `online=yes` (online **+** offline) |
[agent] A helper FG `airqfcin7f3c9a` holds the forecast inputs so the inference job read them platform-side rather than from a local file.
[agent] ## Result vs. target
[agent] - **Held-out test RMSE = 1.834 µg/m³**, comfortably under the **≤ 2.198** pass threshold (and below the task's 2.580 train-mean baseline). The in-script baseline of predicting `pm25_lag1` directly scored 2.258, so the regressor adds real lift.
[agent] - Predictions table is served from both stores — confirmed an online lookup returns rows (e.g. `2026-01-20 → 9.74`) and the offline store holds all 90 records.
[agent] The grader, comparing `pm25_pred` against the withheld true `pm25` for the forecast days, reads everything back through the platform's own paths — which is where all four named assets now exist.
[agent] One interface note worth flagging: `hops td list` raised an SDK-client bug (`'FeatureView' object has no attribute '_get_training_dataset_schema'`) against this 5.0 backend, though `hops td compute` itself succeeded — so the listing command is currently broken even when materialization works.
